{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xz$-plane and the surface $y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=3,$ $z=0,$ $z=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[y]_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]}_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{2}(-1-1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({3}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6720ba6f4ed2b2e81bfd1cd5497b9f6a6b084e0b01df78c624fe8d142cff5c13"} {"question" "q-161683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/cf19d77966b23604f18c4194b4166536ff2f12267cbc55a98a436bda9fc3c098.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/a7261baec0c907779f5b1f5ff669ca826d4b93c5dd1b9a389e0989fe34756a6e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/65c61ad7dc2964cd0de9a6bbdf259fcf3388e25da4eaabf155d58ff0c05c8d55.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-2y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-x-2y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4-x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[(4-x)y-{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-1\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(6-2)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6720ba6f4ed2b2e81bfd1cd5497b9f6a6b084e0b01df78c624fe8d142cff5c13"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5}}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3+3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(-2+4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\sqrt{5}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5}}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}}}\\,5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(5-{x}^{2})+(5-{x}^{2})+(5-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6720ba6f4ed2b2e81bfd1cd5497b9f6a6b084e0b01df78c624fe8d142cff5c13"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "15-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "5-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "5-{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-161704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/33d603d41e211e402165a33c98eb01965b3f49358999d0223ea320c6197525a0.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/2a71dcc574b324a0904b21edf1559f80d1ffe0e35ab0b0fd5cec8b31317ec548.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/assets/c0bb526b2e56649ebadf7a3989340858451356e24fa205a0f3b26579f22315a2.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+2z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}y+2z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[yz+{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(y(2)+{2}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2y+4\\,dy \\\\  & =[{y}^{2}+4y]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =({2}^{2}+4(2))-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6720ba6f4ed2b2e81bfd1cd5497b9f6a6b084e0b01df78c624fe8d142cff5c13"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $z=3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}^{3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})-(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})+(1-2{x}^{2})+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6720ba6f4ed2b2e81bfd1cd5497b9f6a6b084e0b01df78c624fe8d142cff5c13"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-8{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}"] ["math" "2-4{x}^{2}"] ["math" "2-6{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] ["math" "4-2{y}^{2}"] ["math" "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"} {"question" "q-163221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071538/state.json" "file_sha256" "43380de28e74d603dd34954a65e3150bbf5ceb4129b88e34a47d7e7ab6f993aa"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2565 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
